{
  "id": "c1-e46-access-for-all",
  "level": "C1",
  "version": 1,
  "topic": "Access for all",
  "parts": [
    {
      "index": 1,
      "title": "Interview",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p1-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Good afternoon. First of all, we'd like to know a little about you.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p1-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4500
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q1",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, how accessible do you think your town is for people with disabilities?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p1-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5900
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q2",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, have you ever had difficulty getting around because of a temporary injury?",
          "durationSec": 25,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p1-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 6100
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q3",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "text": "Candidate A, what do you think inclusion means?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p1-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 3600
        },
        {
          "id": "p1-q4",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "text": "Candidate B, do you think the way we design public places has changed?",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p1-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5200
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 2,
      "title": "Long turn",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p2-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "In this part of the test, I'm going to give each of you three pictures. I'd like you to talk about two of them on your own for about a minute, and also to answer a question briefly about your partner's pictures.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p2-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 13200
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "c1-e46-a1",
            "c1-e46-a2",
            "c1-e46-a3"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate A, your pictures show people facing obstacles. Choose two of the pictures and say what difficulties these people might experience, and what could be done to help them.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p2-a.mp3",
          "audioMs": 11700
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-a-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate B, which of these obstacles do you think is easiest to overcome?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p2-a-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5700
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "assets": [
            "c1-e46-b1",
            "c1-e46-b2",
            "c1-e46-b3"
          ],
          "text": "Candidate B, your pictures show efforts to make places accessible. Choose two of the pictures and say what difference these measures might make, and how people might react.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p2-b.mp3",
          "audioMs": 11400
        },
        {
          "id": "p2-b-follow",
          "kind": "turn",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 30,
          "text": "Candidate A, who should pay for making public places accessible?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p2-b-follow.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4700
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 3,
      "title": "Collaborative task",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p3-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like you to talk about something together for about two minutes. Here are some ways of making society more inclusive, and a question for you to discuss.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p3-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 10500
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-discuss",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 120,
          "diagram": "c1-e46-access-for-all",
          "text": "Talk to each other about this question: How might these measures help people with disabilities to take part fully in society?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p3-discuss.mp3",
          "audioMs": 9000
        },
        {
          "id": "p3-decide",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 60,
          "diagram": "c1-e46-access-for-all",
          "text": "Now you have about a minute to decide together. Which would make the biggest difference?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p3-decide.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5700
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "index": 4,
      "title": "Discussion",
      "steps": [
        {
          "id": "p4-intro",
          "kind": "narration",
          "text": "Now I'd like to ask you some more questions about accessibility and inclusion.",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p4-intro.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5800
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q1",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "To what extent is society responsible for removing barriers faced by people with disabilities?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p4-q1.mp3",
          "audioMs": 7300
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q2",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, should children with special needs be taught in ordinary schools?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p4-q2.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5600
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q3",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, do you think employers are afraid of hiring people with disabilities?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p4-q3.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5900
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q4",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "both",
          "durationSec": 50,
          "text": "Could technology be the key to a fully inclusive society?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p4-q4.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4400
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q5",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "A",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate A, how can ordinary people become more aware of the needs of others?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p4-q5.mp3",
          "audioMs": 5700
        },
        {
          "id": "p4-q6",
          "kind": "open",
          "target": "B",
          "durationSec": 45,
          "text": "Candidate B, do laws alone make a society more inclusive?",
          "audio": "audio/C1/c1-e46-access-for-all/p4-q6.mp3",
          "audioMs": 4800
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
